{"name":"Mecca Orange","hex":"#bd5745","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mecca","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of Mecca.\n; a place to which a group of people (for example shoppers) are drawn.","; a place to which a group of people (for example shoppers) are drawn."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mecca"},{"term":"orange","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An evergreen tree of the genus Citrus such as Citrus sinensis which yields oranges (the fruit).","Any round citrus fruit with a yellow-red colour when ripe and a sour-sweet taste; the fruit of the orange tree.\n Specifically, a sweet orange or Citrus sinensis."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having the colour of the fruit of an orange tree; yellowred; reddish-yellow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orange"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mecca","blocks":[{"text":"Mecca, officially Makkah al-Mukarramah, is a city in the Hejaz region of western Saudi Arabia and is the capital of Mecca Province. Mecca is considered the birthplace of Islam and the Islamic prophet Muhammad, as well as being the holiest city in Islam."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Great_Mosque_of_Mecca1.jpg/330px-Great_Mosque_of_Mecca1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mecca","wikidata":"Q5806"},{"title":"Orange (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Orange is the colour between yellow and red on the spectrum of visible light. The human eyes perceive orange when observing light with a dominant wavelength between roughly 585 and 620 nanometres. In traditional colour theory, it is a secondary colour of pigments, produced by mixing yellow and red. In the RGB colour model, it is a tertiary colour. It is named after the fruit of the same name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Delicatearch.png/330px-Delicatearch.png?utm_s